index 00000000..c5270c15
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/EXIT_CODES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# Startup exit codes
+
+The runtime returns a small, stable set of process exit codes so a launcher
+can name the failure instead of showing one generic "the game did not start".
+They are declared in `runtime/include/psx_exit_codes.h`.
+
+| Code | Name | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| 0 | `PSX_EXIT_OK` | Normal quit / clean end of a session. |
+| 1 | `PSX_EXIT_ERROR` | Unclassified error. Keep this for crash reports. |
+| 2 | `PSX_EXIT_USAGE` | A command-line argument was malformed. |
+| 3 | `PSX_EXIT_GAME_CONFIG` | Missing or invalid `game.toml` / regional config. |
+| 4 | `PSX_EXIT_NO_DISC` | No disc image was selected. |
+| 5 | `PSX_EXIT_DISC_UNREADABLE` | The disc image could not be opened or read. |
+| 6 | `PSX_EXIT_WRONG_DISC` | The image is not this title's expected disc/region. |
+| 7 | `PSX_EXIT_SBI_REQUIRED` | The disc needs its matching `.sbi` companion. |
+| 8 | `PSX_EXIT_DISC_MOUNT` | The image opened but the CD-ROM layer could not mount it. |
+| 9 | `PSX_EXIT_BIOS` | The selected BIOS could not be activated. |
+| 10 | `PSX_EXIT_MOD_PLAN` | The selected mod plan could not be resolved or activated. |
+| 11 | `PSX_EXIT_RENDERER` | The window/graphics backend could not be created. |
+
+## `[game] strict_disc_id`
+
+A readable disc whose serial does not match the title used to warn and boot
+anyway. With:
+
+```toml
+[game]
+strict_disc_id = true
+```
+
+the runtime refuses it with `PSX_EXIT_WRONG_DISC` and prints/launcher-shows the
+identity warning. Multi-disc sets are still checked disc by disc through
+`[game] disc_serials`. Titles that accept several regions, or deliberately
+boot odd images, simply leave the key out (the default).
+
+## Launcher use
+
+A launcher can map the codes it knows to one-line messages and leave 1
+unmapped so unexpected failures still produce a crash report. The codes never
+replace a successful session's 0, and no code is reused for a different
+meaning.
