@@ -1399,3 +1399,22 @@ callbacks. Address collisions or capacity failures reject the launch through
 always-on direct implementations. Every session rearms its selected plan.
 Replacement overrides cannot be selected as netplay local-view plugins: they
 change shared execution rather than only sandboxed presentation.
+
+## Launcher session overrides
+
+A launcher that owns a game page can start an install with a feature set or
+option values different from the player's saved `mods/state.toml`, without
+rewriting that file. Pass either flag (repeatable) before the first mod
+commit:
+
+```
+--mod-feature <package>/<feature>=on|off
+--mod-option <package>/<feature>/<option>=<value>
+```
+
+The runtime resolves the plan over a copy of the player's selection, applies
+the overrides through the same catalog validation as the launcher ABI, and
+restores the saved selection before `install_plan()` persists it. Overrides
+therefore apply to the session only; `mods/state.toml` stays the player's.
+Unknown package, feature or option ids fail the launch with
+`PSX_EXIT_MOD_PLAN` instead of being ignored.
